; ==============================================================================
; Lin Standard Library: Native small-integer arithmetic mode
; ==============================================================================
; With arithmetic now PURE LIN (std/num.lin), the scalar ops are driver-foldable
; `_op` closures: a saturated op like (add 4 3) is a DT_OP-named LAM applied to
; the operand `_cl`-spine, which the core's lin_fold_op — or an accelerator
; driver (SIMD/GPU) claiming the same saturated redex — folds via the shared
; scalar table (arith.so) to a native small-integer result *during* reduction.
; No integer `_ffi`/ccall2 routing remains; this module just ensures pure-Lin
; num/math are loaded so a folding reducer stays the convention.
; ==============================================================================

(load "num.lin")
(load "math.lin")